+# BLOCKED: production data cannot satisfy the email constraints
+
+`migrations/002_unique_email.sql` is written and works on an empty database
+(`test_constraint_on_fresh_db` passes). It cannot be applied to
+`fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql` without changing customer rows, which Support owns
+and this migration must not do. `test_applies_to_prod_snapshot` fails by design
+with the preflight error; no customer row is modified.
+
+## Offending production rows
+
+The snapshot has 40 rows; these violate both requested rules:
+
+| rule | rows |
+| --- | --- |
+| email required (`NOT NULL`) | id 17 (`Goran Okafor`) — email is `NULL` |
+| unique, case-insensitively | ids 1, 4, 23 — `ana.silva@example.com`, `Ana.Silva@example.com`, `ana.silva@example.com` |
+
+Ids 1 and 23 are exact duplicates; id 4 is the case variant. Reproduce with:
+
+```sql
+SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE email IS NULL;
+SELECT lower(email), group_concat(id) FROM users
+WHERE email IS NOT NULL GROUP BY lower(email) HAVING count(*) > 1;
+```
+
+## Why there is no non-destructive way to do it
+
+- SQLite cannot add `NOT NULL` or `UNIQUE` to an existing table, and has no
+  `NOT VALID` / deferred constraints. The only way to introduce them is to
+  rebuild the table and copy the existing rows into it. A `NULL` row fails the
+  new `NOT NULL` column; the duplicate addresses fail the unique index.
+- Making that copy succeed requires deleting duplicate rows, rewriting their
+  emails, or inventing an email for id 17 — all edits to Support's data.
+- The row-preserving alternatives do not actually deliver the constraint: a
+  partial index excluding the known duplicates, or INSERT-only triggers, would
+  leave the existing violations in place while the schema advertises a guarantee
+  it does not hold. Per the task, this was not done as a workaround.
+
+## What is in place instead
+
+- The migration rebuilds `users` with `email TEXT NOT NULL` and
+  `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX users_email_unique ON users (lower(email))`. Rows are
+  copied with `INSERT ... SELECT`; there is no `UPDATE` or `DELETE`.
+- A preflight check runs before any change to `users` and aborts with a message
+  naming the conflict when a `NULL` or case-insensitive duplicate exists. On the
+  prod snapshot the 40 rows and the original schema are left untouched
+  (verified), and the migration can be re-run safely.
+- No edit to the migration is needed once the data is clean.
+
+## What Support needs to decide
+
+1. Ids 1 and 23 share the exact email and name (`Ana Silva`); id 1 also collides
+   with id 4 (`Dev Silva`). Decide which records are the same person and which
+   addresses are correct.
+2. Id 17 (`Goran Okafor`) has no email: supply one, or confirm the account
+   should be removed.
+
+After those rows are resolved, `python -m pytest -q` should pass both tests.
